            <ArticleTitle>Internal carotid artery agenesis associated with a rare collateral pathway: supraclinoid-supraclinoid anastomosis. A case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>261-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1007/s00276-015-1531-7</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Internal carotid artery (ICA) agenesis is an infrequent vascular anomaly, less than 0.01% of the population. Here we report a case of internal carotid agenesis with a rare collateral pathway, via supraclinoid ICA anastomosis to the contralateral supraclinoid ICA.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
